<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 48,558 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 48,558 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 48,558 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 77,885 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   May 20</p>
<p>    Export cargo		19,565	 4,880</p>
<p>    Import cargo		28,993	73,005</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, three are expected to sail and five are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	  7,000	 Patty Anne		22/5</p>
<p>Vegoil		 18,000	 Ariston		   22/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     25,000	 Jaguar		    Due</p>
<p>Chemical		3,000	 Bow Sea		   25/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
